<%- include("partials/head") %>
<%- include("partials/header") %>
<%- include("partials/nav") %>

<main class="resume-layout">
  <%- include("partials/contactModal") %>

  <article class="project-detail">
    <header class="card project-detail-hero">
      <a href="/projects" class="project-back-link">Back to projects</a>
      <p class="project-tag">School Team Project · Next.js / Vercel</p>
      <h1>Handcrafted Haven</h1>
      <p>
        A school team project for a marketplace-style web app where artisans can
        present handmade products and visitors can browse products, sellers and
        reviews. My contribution was focused on helping the final version come
        together, not on claiming the whole app as a solo build.
      </p>

      <div class="project-detail-actions">
        <a
          href="https://handcrafted-haven-blush.vercel.app/"
          class="project-link project-link-primary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          Live Demo
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/STU6266/handcrafted-haven"
          class="project-link project-link-secondary"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="project-detail-media-grid project-detail-media-grid--compact" aria-label="Handcrafted Haven visuals">
      <figure class="project-media-card">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/handcrafted-haven/home.png"
          alt="Handcrafted Haven desktop homepage showing marketplace intro, navigation and how it works cards"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Desktop homepage and marketplace intro</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="project-media-card">
        <img
          src="/images/projects/handcrafted-haven/mobile.png"
          alt="Handcrafted Haven mobile homepage with responsive navigation and marketplace content"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Mobile responsive homepage</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="project-detail-grid">
      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Handcrafted Haven was built as a school group project. The app
          presents a handmade-product marketplace concept with product browsing,
          seller pages, product details, ratings/reviews and seller-only product
          listing workflows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>Tech Stack</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Next.js, TypeScript and React-style page structure</li>
          <li>Node.js backend pieces with database-backed project goals</li>
          <li>MongoDB/Mongoose listed in the project stack</li>
          <li>Vercel deployment and GitHub Projects for organization</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>My Role</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Team project for school, not a solo fullstack build</li>
          <li>Helped with integration and Vercel deployment support</li>
          <li>Worked on cleanup, small bug fixes and final stabilization</li>
          <li>Supported accessibility/usability improvements and smoke checks</li>
          <li>Helped with project-board tasks and coordination</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="card project-detail-section">
        <h2>What It Shows</h2>
        <p>
          This project is useful in the portfolio because it shows that I can
          work inside a team codebase, help organize a project toward delivery,
          support deployment and improve the quality of a final version without
          overstating my individual contribution.
        </p>
      </section>
    </section>
  </article>
</main>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
